untry>JP</country><doc-number>7300458</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8151559-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8151559</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4626497-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4626497</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations> <non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1046657A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAGIWARA TSUNEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMURA YORIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TEIJIN SEIKI CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAGIWARA, TSUNEO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, YORIKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIJIN SEIKI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAGIWARA TSUNEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMURA YORIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAGIWARA, TSUNEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, YORIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A photocurable resin composition capable of giving, e.g., a three-dimensional shape which is reduced in volumetric shrinkage and excellent in dimensional accuracy, has a high heat distortion temperature and excellent heat resistance, and is excellent in transparency and mechanical properties. The composition comprises (i) at least one imidized acrylic compound represented by formula (I) (wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents an optionally substituted alicyclic, aromatic, or aliphatic group; R&lt;2&gt; represents a residue of an amino alcohol; R&lt;3&gt; represents hydrogen or methyl; and n is 1 or 2), (ii) a radical-polymerizable compound and/or cationically polymerizable compound which each is a compound other than the imidized acrylic compound, and (iii) a photopolymerization initiator. The proportion of the component (i) to the component (ii) is 80/20 to 10/90 (by weight).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition résineuse photopolymérisable permettant la formation d'un profilé tridimensionnel dont le retrait volumétrique est réduit et la précision dimensionnelle excellente et présentant des propriétés de transparence et mécaniques excellentes. Ladite composition comporte: (i) au moins un composé acrylique imidé représenté par la formule (I) (dans laquelle R&lt;1&gt; représente un groupe alicyclique, aromatique ou aliphatique éventuellement substitué; R&lt;2&gt; représente un reste d'amino-alcool; R&lt;3&gt; représente hydrogène ou méthyle; et n vaut 1 ou 2); (ii) un composé pouvant être polymérisé par polymérisation radicalaire et/ou un composé polymérisable par polymérisation cationique, chaque composé étant différent du composé acrylique imidé, et (iii) un amorceur de photopolymérisation. Le rapport pondéral entre le composant (i) et le composant (ii) est de 80/20 à 10/90 (en poids).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>